{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6bef4a923833d9eb","name":"Corellian HWK-290 Light Freighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-6bef4a923833d9eb","title":"Corellian HWK-290 Light Freighter","revision":19407,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:54:54Z","sha256":"40bd8c6a22c6cc5cfb049adfd3bfc77df694f498f3a7e65f34d7624f7059f8b0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19407","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Corellian%20HWK-290%20Light%20Freighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6bef4a923833d9eb","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Corellian Engineering Corporation designed the Hawk series of transports in the decades before ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", in an effort to break into a new market for small, fast cargo ships. Although the YT-series of ships was wildly successful financially, it was seen by the galaxy at large as being rugged but ugly- tramp ships for tramp captains. The Hawk line was aimed at more upscale clients- wealthy merchants in need of ships to land at resort worlds without being an eyesore, and nobles or politicians in need of a cargo craft for personal business that wouldn't lower their prestige. The line was a modest success, but never hit sales numbers to rival YT-series ships, and it was discontinued during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," to make way for more military production.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The HWK-290 is the most prevalent of the Hawk-series of freighters, and a common sight through ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," and the first few decades of the New Order. It is extremely nimble for a cargo vessel, depending on maneuverability rather than strong shields or armor to survive attack. Stock versions of the ship have no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},", but as with most CEC models, it's easy to add a few lasers as modifications. (Linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannons"}," are the most common addition, and two sets are included in the statistics here.) Ships actually intended for military use (such as The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Moldy Crow"]},", used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kyle Katarn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kyle_Katarn","referenceId":"reference:71f9e86450d44ffa"}," among others) can carry more than twice as many weapons, though at the expense of some cargo capacity.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Corellian HWK-290 Light Freighter Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +0; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28; +12 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https: